    "A burst is one process opening one channel and, on one thread, publishing and consuming each message as fast as the SDK takes the calls, or held to a paced schedule.",
    "A recorded burst\u0027s recorded calls are the publications and consumptions the session it published holds, as icat messages derives them; a capture that could not keep them all says so in its health, as icat record does, and is never read as having kept them.",
